# fi, "in/at", and its contractions with the definite article, which carry the
# same sun-letter assimilation as the bare article: fil-, fis-, fit-, fiċ-,
# fid-, fin-, fir-, fix-, fiz-, fiż-, and fl- before a vowel.  "Fis-sebgħa"
# ("at seven") is the ordinary way to state a clock time.
# en.wiktionary.org, fi; languagephrases.com, "Telling Time In Maltese
# Language".
